"comments": {
"@0bajtm5c3akp9kv2eokn7kplu4": "A span element with these children: a run of text inside a line.",
"@11egf8qi4m8uiisg4s9i3pdfbo": "A p element with these children: a paragraph.",
"@1dlc3j1r4c8lejmpugqkah870a": "An element with these children, for a tag that has no function of its own here (main, nav, table, …). Each tag a function, as in Elm's Html module (prior art).",
"@4ftt6b54pb8e4tfh528aoliovi": "A h2 element with these children: a second-level heading.",
"@95up53v5bherj0vofl6j56r32t": "A style element holding these rules.",
"@bnt6frlli5m0jmk1pbsj7qnapg": "A ul element with these children: a list with bullets, whose items are li.",
"@c07e3r18tto2j84pvfj22efpn9": "An input field: it has attributes and no children.",
"@cn1bj3u9h49b0qt78ru8tvsj1n": "The same element with these attributes added after its own. Text and parts have no attributes, so they come back as they are.",
"@d7k7nj7ltc7ebq2fr7f17bkb3l": "The same element in this class, for a style sheet's rules to select.",
"@fsm6etn1drvap7h6p3hap1o99f": "The same element with this id.",
"@gg9ph94gro3kinrkpvutrp3bco": "A button with this label that runs then when it's clicked.",
"@i4bmujr86b3j9mit11ndt8pka2": "A section element with these children: a part of the page.",
"@i9664ka5vohal8fq60j7t06k2n": "Text that doesn't change. Text that does is text(() => …), which the page runs again when what it reads changes.",
"@l1ibnd69fhv5j8j3reredg1ar1": "A style sheet rule: a selector and its declarations. A style sheet is a list of these, so it shows rule by rule instead of as one long text.",
"@nkrf9fpmaofjbk2gapm71iios9": "A div with these children. To give it attributes, wrap it: styled, classed, with.",
"@p41hp9utbraclqe3msq6j9oklq": "A footer element with these children: the page's foot.",
"@p5apbbq9ngorqb6m3hg3ruufc4": "A h1 element with these children: the biggest heading.",
"@qbot4e096sahnr1mdu2555a3q2": "A li element with these children: one item of a list.",
"@qg6dvr53pobhnh5bg3qf3i94kc": "A label element with these children: a label for a field.",
"@rrc61bud51hgr319omhcik166b": "The texts with between between each two of them.",
"@ssahikkgqdgj9h38blqbk0bq0s": "An attribute whose value doesn't change.",
"@tucbcblcvkuen34hb5ao1gb2co": "A strong element with these children: important text, usually bold.",
"@urmvgd3e2dcctt7q85g15nql15": "Rules that apply only when the query holds, such as (prefers-color-scheme: dark).",
"@v4m3u10hkehjb5097mejohqi5p": "A length in pixels, from a Float64 or an Int.",
"@vs2r19tn6qo91rsltkdmc3cj24": "The items of a cell's list, each drawn by row and all put inside (ul, div, …). An item still there when the list changes keeps its row as it was; only new items get one. Solid's <For> (prior art).",
"@vtbglf9bi4e1skn05c8d1is91q": "The same element with this inline style (CSS declarations, such as color: #777; margin: 0)."
},
